Description: Keep the prebuilt libraries in the source package.
 The NPU engines are prebuilt libraries in src/lib, which the build links. dpkg-source leaves files named like build
 output, *.so and *.a among them, out of a source package of format 3.0 by default, so the source package built from
 the source tree lacked them and its build failed to link. An explicit tar-ignore replaces that default list, and leaves
 out only the directories of git, which a checkout has.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/source/options
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+tar-ignore = .git
